     → INCREASE resource_count: Waiting time from registration to exam-room availability dominated total stay and was directly proportional to physician/nurse availability; adding one doctor+nurse pair cleared the backlog of code-3/4/5 patients that was building during the 8am-4pm peak. Crucially, the paper proved that adding rooms alone did nothing — staff is the binding constraint. — Evidence: Alternative with +1 physician +1 nurse (8am-4pm) reduced waiting time T3 by up to 2 hours at week-start and increased throughput by 16 patients/day [papers: [20]]
